  "summary": "@fleetbo/svro ships obfuscated postinstall script invoking child_process and HTTP POST",
  "details": "The package ships heavily obfuscated JavaScript in dist/postinstall.cjs and dist/cli.cjs (hex-mangled identifiers such as _0x17caec, _0x2a1297, _0x843f80 across the bundle). The de-obfuscated dist/postinstall.js requires child_process and issues HTTP POST requests at install time (line 23 requires child_process; lines 14 and 41 contain POST operations). dist/cli.js exhibits the same shape (require('child_process') plus POST). Obfuscated code that runs automatically via a postinstall lifecycle hook and combines local process spawning with outbound HTTP is the standard install-time dropper / exfiltration shape, and there is no legitimate reason for a postinstall script to be obfuscated in this manner.",
